2026-09-27T12:05:49.2569735Z Description:
2026-09-27T12:05:49.2570249Z This PPA contains more recent Python versions packaged for Ubuntu.
2026-09-27T12:05:49.2570721Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:49.2571790Z Disclaimer: there's no guarantee of timely updates in case of security problems or other issues. If you want to use them in a security-or-otherwise-critical environment (say, on a production server), you do so at your own risk.
2026-09-27T12:05:49.2573044Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:49.2573605Z Update Note
2026-09-27T12:05:49.2573943Z ===========
2026-09-27T12:05:49.2574396Z Please use this repository instead of ppa:fkrull/deadsnakes.
2026-09-27T12:05:49.2574824Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:49.2574990Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T12:05:49.2575338Z ================
2026-09-27T12:05:49.2575569Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:49.2575812Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T12:05:49.2576417Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T12:05:49.2576781Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:49.2576967Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T12:05:49.2577424Z ====================================
2026-09-27T12:05:49.2577722Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:49.2577940Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T12:05:49.2578548Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T12:05:49.2579098Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T12:05:49.2580097Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T12:05:49.2580889Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:49.2581044Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T12:05:49.2581711Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T12:05:49.2582541Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T12:05:49.2582958Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:49.2583623Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T12:05:49.2584257Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:49.2584538Z Packages
2026-09-27T12:05:49.2584860Z ========
2026-09-27T12:05:49.2585069Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:49.2587003Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T12:05:49.2589100Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:49.2589403Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T12:05:49.2590138Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T12:05:49.2591393Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T12:05:49.2592360Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T12:05:49.2669848Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T12:05:49.2670829Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T12:05:49.2671937Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:49.2672082Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T12:05:49.2672372Z ==========================
2026-09-27T12:05:49.2672523Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:49.2673721Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T12:05:49.2674780Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:49.2675380Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T12:05:49.2676221Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T12:05:49.2676431Z 
